BEGIN_DESC
TANTRA BETA 10 - Moon, EMPU at Brighton Beach (crew platform, look C "exoskeleton").
EMPU = the MPU chassis with the crew module: a framed nose (its lower panes show the ground at the front wheels), the pressure
hull in an external load frame, the system bays over the fenders (gases, CO2, water on the left; the thermal loop and heaters on
the right), radiators stowed on the roof, a solar panel and the mast; the airlock in the stern.
BOARDING: walk to the stern door's stairs - F enters the airlock. The inner door leads into the habitat (the passage is open).
Inside: two seats at the console (the driver's on the left, with the yoke), four bunks on the right, a table with two benches and
the galley on the left. The cabin holds shirt-sleeve air: K takes the suit off.
SEATS: F at a seat sits down; F again stands up. In the driver's seat the hands go to the yoke and the driver's keys drive:
W forward (40 km/h), Shift+W full power (80 km/h), A/D steer, S service brake / reverse, Space emergency brake, B parking brake,
Caps Lock deck up / down, V the EMPU from outside. Leaving: F by the stern door inside the airlock - out at the foot of the stairs.
CONTEXT ACTIONS (look at a part, wheel to pick, F to do): the power socket and the four energy cells (right side), the couplings.
END_DESC

